<title>GERMANY: Most Germans doubt euro will come on time -- poll.</title>
<headline>Most Germans doubt euro will come on time -- poll.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most Germans do not believe Europe's planned single currency will get under way as scheduled on January 1, 1999, according to a magazine poll released on Sunday.</p>
<p>Sixty percent of those questioned for the news magazine Der Spiegel said they did not believe the project would start on time, while 39 percent believed it would.</p>
<p>Polling firm Emnid interviewed 1,384 people between June 17 and 20 for the poll, which Spiegel released ahead of publication in Monday's edition.</p>
